# Build context for the streamer release image (docker/streamer/Dockerfile, repo root context).
#
# What goes in: the Rust workspace, Cargo.lock, rust-toolchain.toml and the two licence texts —
# the release build needs nothing else. Everything below stays out, so the context stays small, a
# stale build output or a node_modules tree can never reach an image layer, and no machine-local
# setting (`.env`) can be baked into a published artefact.
#
# Each name is listed in both spellings (`x` and `**/x`): a directory of that name is excluded
# wherever it sits. A new build context with a different root needs its own file — docker/dev and
# docker/spike build from their own directories and never see this one.

# git, and the files that only the repository's own tooling reads
.git
.github
.gitattributes
.gitignore
.editorconfig
AGENTS.md

# Rust build output, in whatever form it exists
target
**/target
build
**/build

# The TypeScript workspace: its install, its output and its configuration. Not part of the Rust
# build, and node_modules through a Windows bind mount is exactly what should never travel.
node_modules
**/node_modules
dist
**/dist
*.tsbuildinfo
packages
eslint.config.js
pnpm-lock.yaml
pnpm-workspace.yaml
tsconfig.base.json

# Documents, diagrams, branding, and the manual spike artefacts
docs
assets
artifacts
**/artifacts
*.md

# Machine-local settings. Never in an image.
.env
.env.*
